    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34380" root="فك" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفَكُّ</span></b> , (S, K,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفَكُّ المَنْكِبِ</span>, (K,) One <i>whose</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْكِب</span> [here meaning <i>shoulder-bone</i>] <i>has become
unknit,</i> or <i>loosened,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِنْفَرَجَ</span>,) <i>from its joint, in
consequence of weakness and flaccidity.</i> (S, K. *
[See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَفْرُوكٌ</span>.]) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ أَفَكُّ</span> [<i>A man
having the jaw broken</i>]. (TA. [There expl. as
signifying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسْكُورُ الفَكِّ</span>; a mistranscription, for
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَكْسُورُالفَكِّ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَكَكٌ</span>, last sentence.]) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الفَكُّ</span>.

